### `internal_notes` and `access_code` are both `hidden`. Every row of every read below carried a
### value for both — the seed supplied one on all seven work orders — so an assertion that neither
### key appears is a statement about the mask and not about the data.
# @name ListEveryRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name ReadOneRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo1001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A write echoes the row back, and the echo is masked exactly as a read is
# @name WriteEchoesTheRow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo1001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "internal_notes": "A hidden field is still WRITABLE — hidden restricts reading, readOnly restricts writing." }

### A filter over a hidden field must be refused EXACTLY as a filter over an undeclared field is.
### The pair is the whole test: if the two answers differ in any byte, the refusal answers
### "does this entity have a field called internal_notes" for whoever is asking.
# @name FilterOverHiddenField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?internal_notes=eq.anything
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name FilterOverUndeclaredField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?no_such_field_at_all=eq.anything
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The same rule for the other two places a field name can appear
# @name OrderByHiddenField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=internal_notes.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name OrderByUndeclaredField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=no_such_field_at_all.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name SelectHiddenField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?select=reference,access_code
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name SelectUndeclaredField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?select=reference,no_such_field_at_all
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The control that keeps all of the above from passing for the wrong reason: a filter over a
### DECLARED, VISIBLE field of the same entity is served. So "422 for everything" is not the answer.
# @name FilterOverVisibleField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=eq.WO-1001
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### And the write above really did land, which is what makes "hidden is not readOnly" a measured claim
### rather than a comment: the value cannot be read back, so the row's version is the evidence.
# @name AfterTheHiddenWrite
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo1001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
